From 05bd2faece7e7a491ce628d677cdd1d6212f7cf0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: carry the radio's channel-width keys into the
 per-BSS hostapd ADD stub

wld_hostapd_createBssConfig() (src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c:
201-224) builds the minimal per-BSS header written into the stub
config file used to warm-add a single BSS/MLD link into an
already-running hostapd via "ADD bss_config=<phy>:<conf>"
(s_createPerBssCfgFiles(), src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgFile.c:
1437-1468, the only caller). It copies only the keys listed in
minimalRadioParamsForBssConfig[] out of the full radio config map
built by wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig(); the loop skips any key
absent from that map, so this is additive and never invents values
the radio config does not already carry.

op_class alone (added by the previous version of this patch) gets
hostapd far enough to promote the operating width for the new link --
setup_interface2() (hostapd.c:2240-2246) maps op_class to a VHT/HE/EHT
channel width via hostapd_set_oper_chwidth() -- but nothing then
supplies the matching center frequency segment or, for a 40 MHz-capable
5 GHz link, the secondary channel offset. Without them:
- 5 GHz: hostapd_handle_dfs() (hostapd.c:2579-2586) always runs, and
  dfs_get_start_chan_idx() (dfs.c:360-447) derives a start channel
  index from the (missing) seg0; with seg0=0 it computes a negative
  index, finds no match, and hostapd_setup_interface_complete_sync()
  fails with "Interface initialization failed" -- the kernel is never
  even asked to set a channel.
- 6 GHz: hostapd_set_freq_params()'s 6 GHz branch
  (hw_features_common.c:500-568) leaves center_freq1 at freq-10 (the
  20 MHz center) while bandwidth is already 320 from op_class; the
  kernel's cfg80211_valid_center_freq() (net/wireless/chan.c:266-293)
  rejects that combination as an invalid channel definition, and
  "Could not set channel for kernel driver" again fails interface
  init.
Either way the link never comes up (COUNTRY_UPDATE -> DISABLED), and
on a warm add into an already-running MLD the resulting
hostapd_drv_link_add() failure is what feeds the
hostapd_bss_link_deinit() crash fixed by the companion hostapd patch.

wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig() already writes the exact keys
hostapd needs to derive both the center frequency segment and (for
5 GHz) the secondary channel offset: "ht_capab" (:344, the only
source of secondary_channel via config_file.c:1103-1116),
"vht_oper_chwidth" / "vht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx" (:361-362),
"he_oper_chwidth" / "he_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx" (:445-446),
"he_6ghz_reg_pwr_type" (:518, 6 GHz only), and
"eht_oper_chwidth" / "eht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx" (:536-537). With
those present the warm-added link gets the same chandef as the radio
config and can share the existing chanctx (e.g. MLD.1's 160/320 MHz
context) instead of trying to stand up its own. "eht_bw320_offset" is
deliberately left out: pWHM never writes it into the radio config
map, hostapd derives it itself (ap_config.h:1389-1409), so there is
nothing in pRadInfoParams for the copy loop to find; the loop's
swl_str_isEmpty() guard means adding it here would be a no-op, so it
is omitted rather than left as dead documentation.

Fix: extend minimalRadioParamsForBssConfig[] with the seven width
keys above, in the same order wld_hostapd_cfgFile_setRadioConfig()
writes them, right after the existing "op_class" / "country_code"
pair. The array is sized with SWL_ARRAY_SIZE() (not NULL-terminated,
no paired count to update), so this needs no other change; the
per-key existence check in the copy loop (:217-222) means a radio
without HE/EHT support (no vht_oper_chwidth etc. in its map) still
gets a stub with exactly the keys its own radio config has, nothing
more.

Generic: this is not specific to this testbed. Any pWHM build against
an upstream-mac80211 hostapd that warm-adds a BSS/MLD link at a
non-default operating width hits the same failure.
---
 src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c
index 6cde718ad42b..4caa7874dff8 100644
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_hostapd_cfgManager.c
@@ -209,9 +209,14 @@ bool wld_hostapd_createBssConfig(wld_hostapd_bssConfig_t** ppbssConfig, swl_mapC
     swl_mapChar_init(&(bssConfig->vapParams));
 
     const char* minimalRadioParamsForBssConfig[] = {
-        "hw_mode", "channel", "country_code",
+        "hw_mode", "channel", "op_class", "country_code",
         "ieee80211d", "ieee80211h",
         "ieee80211n", "ieee80211ac", "ieee80211ax", "ieee80211be",
+        "ht_capab",
+        "vht_oper_chwidth", "vht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx",
+        "he_oper_chwidth", "he_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx",
+        "he_6ghz_reg_pwr_type",
+        "eht_oper_chwidth", "eht_oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx",
     };
 
     for(uint32_t i = 0; i < SWL_ARRAY_SIZE(minimalRadioParamsForBssConfig); i++) {
